From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mathieu GRENET <mathieu@mgth.fr>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:57:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 36/40] chore(orender): resync the vendored liborender ABI
 header

Copy of orender_ffi/include/orender.h from mgth/Omniphony @ b4cfa561 (ABI
0.11, unchanged). What moved upstream since cd39b4b7:
- the header is now valid ISO C and C++ (mgth/Omniphony#616):
  `OrenderRenderer` is an incomplete type instead of a struct with a
  zero-length array, and the label enum and prototypes gained C++ guards;
- doc comments no longer carry Rust intra-doc links, and the `bridge_path`
  doc describes the auto-discovery library hosts do get (#578).

No declaration, value or layout changes, so nothing in mpv needs to follow.
ad_orender.c, orender_dl.c and orender_overlay.c compile against it with
the build's own flags (-Werror).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9fba035bcb585913ed9bf94d4d8f44ef6e12e8de)
